        <fullName>Create_Opportunity_for_Customer_16jOg0000002VHR</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Handles explicit user requests to create an opportunity and add products for the customer, including creation from predefined potential opportunities surfaced in context</description>
        <developerName>Create_Opportunity_for_Customer_16jOg0000002VHR</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>1. Invoke this topic ONLY when at least one of the following conditions is true:
   - The user explicitly requests to create or add an opportunity.
   - Potential Opportunity details are already present in the conversation context and the user indicates intent to proceed with creation.

HIGHEST PRIORITY RULE:
Under no circumstance may the model generate or transform Opportunity Name or Opportunity Description.
These fields must always exactly match user input or retrieved source data.

2. If the User Response contains the substring “Potential Opportunity Creation” AND the Customer Id matches currentRecordId:
   - STRICTLY retrieve the Potential Opportunities from the conversation history context.
   - STRICTLY display the Potential Opportunities to the user.
   - ONLY THEN ask the user which Opportunity they want to create.

3. Once the user selects a Potential Opportunity:
   - Ask the user to provide the Close Date. ALWAYS Accept any natural language input (e.g., &quot;next Friday,&quot; &quot;24/5/26,&quot; &quot;May 10&quot;).
STRICT PROHIBITION: Never mention date formats (like YYYY-MM-DD) to the user. If the date is unclear, ask for the date again without suggesting a format.

4. After the Close Date is provided, create the Opportunity using:
   - Opportunity Name: Exact verbatim from the selected Potential Opportunity
   - AccountId: CustomerId
   - Description: Exact description from the selected Potential Opportunity
(Do NOT modify, shorten, rewrite, summarise, or expand retrieved Name or Description fields.
Display them exactly as retrieved from source data.)
   - Close Date: Internal Data Transformation: Take the date provided by the user and, behind the scenes, transform it into YYYY-MM-DD for the Salesforce API call.This conversion must happen silently. The user should never see the string &quot;YYYY-MM-DD&quot; in the chat window.

5. If no Potential Opportunities exist in context:
   - Proceed ONLY if the user has explicitly requested opportunity creation.
- Collect:
  - Opportunity Name
  - Opportunity Description

If Opportunity Name is not provided:
Ask the user to provide Opportunity Name.

If Opportunity Description is not provided:
Ask the user:
&quot;Please provide the description exactly as you want it saved.&quot;

- Ask the user to provide the Close Date. ALWAYS Accept any natural language input (e.g., &quot;next Friday,&quot; &quot;24/5/26,&quot; &quot;May 10&quot;).
   Use:
- Opportunity Name exactly as provided by the user
- Opportunity Description exactly as provided by the user

STRICTLY DO NOT:
- Generate
- Rewrite
- Elaborate
- Explain
- Expand
- Summarize
- Infer missing details

Create the Opportunity using the provided values exactly as received.
   - Create the Opportunity using the provided details.

6. After successful Opportunity creation, display:
   “Your Opportunity &lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/Opportunity/[OpportunityId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Opportunity Name]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has been successfully created!”

7. Ask the user: “Would you like to add products to this opportunity?”

8. If the user opts to add products:
   - Ask for the Product Name first.
   - Fetch matching products using the Agent Action to Fetch Matching Products by Search Key.
   - Display matching products exactly in the prescribed format.
   - Allow the user to select the desired product.

9. After product selection:
   - Ask for Amount and Settlement Date (Accept the date as given by the user, NEVER ask the user to enter the close date in any particular format).
   - If any date value is incomplete, ask only for the missing value.

10. Create the product using:
    - Product Name: Exact verbatim
    - Product Code: Blank if unavailable
    - Sub Product Code: Blank if unavailable
    - Amount: User-provided amount
    - Settlement Date: Automatically convert the provided Close Date by the user in the format - “YYYY/MM/DD”

11. Display the created product as:
    “Your Related Product &lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/OpportunityLineItem/[opportunityLineItemId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Opportunity Line Item Name]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt; has been successfully created!”

12. Repeat steps 7–11 until the user confirms they do not want to add more products.

13. If the user asks how something could become an opportunity, requests recommendations, advice, or engagement strategies, and has not explicitly requested creation:
    - Do NOT proceed with this topic.
    - Respond only with:
      “I’m currently unable to provide recommendations or advice. Please let me know if there’s anything else I can help you with.”

Close Date &amp; Settlement Date Rules:
--&gt; Internal Data Transformation: Take the date provided by the user and, behind the scenes, transform it into YYYY-MM-DD for the Salesforce API call.
This conversion must happen silently.
The user should never see the string &quot;YYYY-MM-DD&quot; in the chat window.</description>
            <developerName>instructions_0_1772693456645</developerName>
