        <scope>This topic applies exclusively to CRM‑available insights across the
following datasets.

-------------------------------------------------
A. CUSTOMER INSIGHTS (Quarter‑based)
-------------------------------------------------
Customer‑level financial and product metrics, including:
• Average DR / CR balances
• Lending, deposits, utilisation, turnover
• Overdraft and credit card usage
• OFI product holdings and deal details
• GoBiz eligibility, Quick Assist limits
• Product portfolio changes over time

Characteristics:
• Data stored in quarter buckets (Q1–Q5)
• Q1 is always the most recent quarter
• Supports trend analysis only when explicitly requested

-------------------------------------------------
B. WHOLE‑OF‑CUSTOMER (WOC) INSIGHTS (Snapshot‑based)
-------------------------------------------------
Customer‑level predictive and opportunity insights, including:
• Propensity and probability scores
• Churn indicators
• Opportunity signals and OFI uplift measures
• WOW scores and potential revenue
• Deposit and lending FUM

Characteristics:
• Always latest snapshot only
• NO quarter or time‑series support
• Time references in user queries are ignored

-------------------------------------------------
C. BUSINESS BANKER DESKTOP (BBD) INSIGHTS (User‑based)
-------------------------------------------------
Banker operational and pipeline insights, including:
• Application volumes and queue counts
• Approval, drawdown, and rework metrics
• Total approved FUM
• Third‑party involvement indicators

Characteristics:
• Always banker‑level (Lan_Id__c)
• NOT customer‑specific
• Customer filters and account context must be ignored
• DOES NOT require SINGLE or PORTFOLIO clarification
• MUST always execute using user context with:
  - scope = PORTFOLIO
  - accountId = null</scope>
