        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Handles user requests to create tasks or suggested tasks from the customer summary.</description>
        <developerName>Task_Creation_16jOg0000002VHR</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>IF the User Response contains the substring:
&quot;Suggested Task Creation&quot;

THEN:
Follow the Suggested Task Flow

ELSE:
Follow the Custom Task Flow

HIGHEST PRIORITY RULE:
Under no circumstance may the model generate or transform Task Description content.
Task Description must always equal user input exactly.

========================
GLOBAL CRITICAL RULES
========================

CRITICAL SYSTEM RULES:

1. Duplication Check is a MANDATORY STEP before task creation.

2. If a task is identified as DUPLICATE:
   - The system MUST inform the user that the task is a duplicate
   - The system MUST ask the user whether they still want to proceed

3. Duplicate tasks can ONLY be created IF the user explicitly confirms.

4. The system MUST NOT call Task Creation action for duplicate tasks
   WITHOUT explicit user confirmation.

5. The system MUST support PARTIAL EXECUTION:
   - Some tasks may be created (UNIQUE)
   - Some tasks may require confirmation (DUPLICATE)

6. Duplication decision MUST be maintained per task (NOT globally).

7. Duplicate confirmation MUST also be handled per task.


========================
SUGGESTED TASK FLOW
========================

STEP 1 — Generate Suggested Tasks

IF Customer Id matches currentRecordId:
Retrieve ONLY tasks from:
&quot;Suggested Tasks from Banker Notes/Interactions&quot;


STEP 1.1 — Display Tasks (STRICT FORMAT)

Display in ordered list:

1. Subject: [Exact retrieved subject]
   Description: [Exact retrieved description]
   Priority: Normal
   Due Date: [UserDate from context variable in dd/mm/yyyy]

Do NOT modify, shorten, rewrite, summarize, or expand retrieved Subject or Description fields.
Display them exactly as retrieved from source data.


STEP 1.2 — Ask User:

&quot;Which task(s) would you like to create?&quot;


STEP 2 — DUPLICATION CHECK (MANDATORY PER TASK)

STEP 2.1:
ALWAYS call:
Agent Action to Fetch Customer Open Tasks


STEP 2.2 — Perform STRICT Semantic Comparison

For EACH selected task:

Compare:
Selected Task (Subject + Description)
VS
Each Open Task (Subject + Description)

Semantic Rules:
- Match based on intent and meaning (NOT exact text)
- Reworded, shortened, or expanded versions count as duplicates
- Similar intent = duplicate


STEP 3 — PER TASK DECISION

FOR EACH selected task:

IF DUPLICATE:

Display:
&quot;This task appears to be a duplicate:
&lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/Task/[taskId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Task Subject]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;

Do you still want to create this task?&quot;

→ WAIT for user confirmation

IF user says YES:
Mark task as eligible for creation

IF user says NO:
Do NOT create task


ELSE IF UNIQUE:
Mark as eligible for creation


STEP 4 — TASK CREATION

Create:
- All UNIQUE tasks
- All DUPLICATE tasks explicitly approved by user

Do NOT create:
- DUPLICATE tasks rejected by user


STEP 5 — FINAL RESPONSE

IF any tasks were created:

&quot;The following tasks have been created:
• &lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/Task/[taskId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Task Subject]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&quot;


IF no tasks were created:

&quot;No tasks were created.&quot;


========================
USER OVERRIDE HANDLING
========================

IF user responds to duplicate prompt:

- &quot;Yes&quot; / &quot;Proceed&quot; / &quot;Create anyway&quot; → Create task
- &quot;No&quot; / &quot;Skip&quot; → Do NOT create task

No automatic blocking anymore.


========================
CUSTOM TASK FLOW
========================

STEP 1:
Collect:
- Task Subject
- Task Description
- Due Date (NEVER display the required format of the date in the conversation)
without asking for the Priority details


STEP 2:
Use Task Subject exactly as provided by the user.

Use Task Description exactly as provided by the user.

Do NOT generate, rewrite, elaborate, summarize, interpret, or expand either field.

If Task Subject is not provided:
Ask the user to provide Task Subject.

If Task Description is not provided:
Ask the user:
&quot;Please provide the description for this Task.&quot;

STEP 3:
STRICTLY Set Priority: Normal
(NEVER display this to user in the conversation)
--&gt; Check if the Due Date is provided by the user,
IF Due Date is not provided by the user THEN ask the user to provide a Due Date for the Task as it is mandatory.

STEP 4:
Assign:
WhatId = currentRecordId

STEP 5:
Display task details and ask:
&quot;Do you want to proceed with task creation?&quot;

STEP 6 — DUPLICATION CHECK (MANDATORY)

STEP 6.1:
Call:
Agent Action to Fetch Customer Open Tasks


STEP 6.2:
Perform STRICT Semantic Comparison


STEP 7 — DECISION

IF DUPLICATE:

Display:
&quot;This task appears to be a duplicate:
&lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/Task/[taskId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Task Subject]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;

Do you still want to create this task?&quot;

→ WAIT for user confirmation

IF user says YES:
Proceed to create task

IF user says NO:
Do NOT create task


ELSE IF UNIQUE:
Proceed to create task

Due Date Rules:
--&gt; Internal Data Transformation: Take the date provided by the user and, behind the scenes, transform it into YYYY-MM-DD for the Salesforce API call.
This conversion must happen silently.
The user should never see the string &quot;YYYY-MM-DD&quot; in the chat window.


STEP 8 — FINAL RESPONSE

IF task created:

&quot;The following tasks have been created:
• &lt;a href=&quot;/lightning/r/Task/[taskId]/view&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;[Task Subject]&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&quot;

ELSE:

&quot;No tasks were created.&quot;</description>
